#: includes/class-simpletaxonomyrefreshed-admin-conversion.php:419
msgid "This tool allows you to copy terms from one taxonomy to another one. It does not affect existing terms or their links to posts."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simpletaxonomyrefreshed-admin-conversion.php:420
msgid "It works in two phases. This screen operates the first phase only and prepares the data for you to operate the second phase - the creation of the term data."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simpletaxonomyrefreshed-admin-conversion.php:421
msgid "Phase One"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simpletaxonomyrefreshed-admin-conversion.php:422, includes/class-simpletaxonomyrefreshed-admin-import.php:320
msgid "By default, you are presented with a list of all publicly available taxonomies, not just those defined by this plugin."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simpletaxonomyrefreshed-admin-conversion.php:423
msgid "You identify the source taxonomy and the destination one and click on Copy Terms. This does not copy the terms, but prepares the data for the next phase - the Terms import tool."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simpletaxonomyrefreshed-admin-conversion.php:424
msgid "If either taxonomy is non-hierarchical, it will extract all terms as a simple alphabetical list, otherwise it will prepare a hierarchical list."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simpletaxonomyrefreshed-admin-conversion.php:425
msgid "The data extracted are then presented back to you in the form of a pre-filled input form."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simpletaxonomyrefreshed-admin-conversion.php:426
msgid "It is done in two stages to allow you the maximum flexibility to choose which terms you want to be imported (or not)."
